    "lawCode": "Add §§4407-a & 4407-b, Ed L",
    "lawSection": "Education Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S441\n\nSPONSOR: HOYLMAN\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the education law, in relation to establishing a dysle-\nxia task force and implementing the findings of such task force\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nTo establish a task force to develop guidelines for appropriate screen-\ning, intervention, and support for students with and at risk of dyslexia\nand related disorders, and to develop a program of study for teachers to\nbetter help students with dyslexia.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 amends the education law by adding two new sections 4407-a and\n4407-b:\n\n44007-a.1 creates the task force on dyslexia within the department to\ndevelop guidelines for the appropriate screening and related disorders,\nprovide guidelines regarding the appropriate interventions and classroom\nsupport for students deemed at risk, and to develop a program of study\nfor teachers to better help students with dyslexia.\n\n4407-a.2 defines the terms dyslexia, screening program, related disor-\nders, and support.\n\n4407-a.3 defines the size, length of service, appointment and service\ncalendar, constituency, and operational details of the task force, and\nrelated details.\n\n4407-a.4 details the topics undertaken by the task force, including\nscreening programs, intervention and classroom support services, guide-\nline development, and program of study development.\n\n4407-a.5 empowers the task force to request studies and or surveys where\nadditional data is needed.\n\n4407-a.6 requires the department to provide staff services to the task\nforce as needed.\n\n4407-a.7 requires at least three public hearings around the state.\n\n4407-a.8 mandates a report submitted to the governor and legislature no\nlater than September 1, 2021 and details some of the required elements\nof the report.\n\n4407-a.9 requires the department to adopt rules and regulations put\nforth by the task force no later that December 31, 2021.\n\n4407-a.10 states nothing in the above section shall require a student\nwith dyslexia to obtain an individualized education program unless the\nstudent has otherwise met the federal conditions necessary.\n\n4407-b.1 defines the terms dyslexia, screening program, related disor-\nders, and support.\n\n4407-b.2 sets the date of no later than July 1, 2022 for each public\nschool to implement screening programs and interventions based on the\ntask force findings.\n\n4407-b.3 requires on or before July 1, 2022 applicants for aò number of\nspecialized educator certifications fulfill a set of requirements\nincluding a complete program of study in the diagnosis and remediation\nof reading and language arts.\n\n4407-a.4 states nothing in the above section shall require a student\nwith dyslexia to obtain an individualized education program unless the\nstudent has otherwise met the federal conditions necessary.\n\nSection 2 Sets an immediate effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nOne in five students has dyslexia or another phonemic awareness issue\nthat requires them to learn to read through a directed multi-sensory\nsequential phonics or Orton-Gillingham approach. The current education\nsystem teaches reading with a balanced literacy approach, which is\nessentially whole language by another name and ineffective at teaching\nreading to the roughly 20% of students who have dyslexia or another\nphonemic based learning difference. This bill will establish a task\nforce to study and implement the best methods to provide these students\nthe classroom resources they require for a lifetime of literacy.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nS.6850 of 2020 (Hoylman): Died in Insurance\n\nA.9023 of 2019-2020 (Simotas): Died in Insurance\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nTo be determined.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediate\n",
